  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1220 PM CDT Thu Oct 8 2026\n\nVery little changes from previous forecasts. Mostly dry conditions \nare expected over land with low to medium rain chances over the Gulf \nwaters through Friday as Tropical Storm Isaias moves away from the \nregion. Although we will not get any direct impacts from Isaias, \nlong period swells are expected through the end of the week are \nexpected to interact with Ekman Transport to promote coastal \nflooding. Apart from the coastal flooding, high risk of rip currents \nwill also be expected. \n\nWarm temperatures will return with highs in the 90s through the week \ninto next week. Thankfully, moisture levels will be low enough to \nkeep the heat index in check through the weekend. Moisture will \nincrease next week with heat index values over 105 degrees returning \nalong with a moderate to major risk of heat-related impacts Monday. \nPlease remember to continue to practice heat safety: take breaks \nwhen outside, drink plenty of water, and look before you lock.",
